    "body": "#### Recall\n\n**1.** 2 : 3\n\n**2.** GH₵1,800 and GH₵2,400\n\n**3.** 72\n\n**4.** GH₵192\n\n**5.** 20 m/s\n\n**6.** 1.21\n\n**7.** 20 litres\n\n**8.** 3 days\n\n#### Key words\n\n**1.** direct\n\n**2.** indirect or inverse\n\n**3.** simple\n\n**4.** compound\n\n**5.** principal\n\n**6.** amount\n\n**7.** With compound interest each year's interest is added to the principal, so the following year's interest is calculated on a larger sum. Simple interest is always worked out on the original amount only.\n\n**8.** 50,000\n\n#### Core practice\n\n**1.** 24 parts; one part GH₵300; shares GH₵1,500, GH₵2,100 and GH₵3,600.\n\n**2.** 4.5 × 50,000 = 225,000 cm = 2.25 km\n\n**3.** 8 km = 800,000 cm; 800,000 ÷ 25,000 = 32 cm\n\n**4.** One book GH₵26, so 11 cost GH₵286.\n\n**5.** Total 60 tap-hours; 60 ÷ 4 = 15 hours.\n\n**6.** I = 4,500 × 8 × 3 ÷ 100 = GH₵1,080; amount GH₵5,580.\n\n**7.** Amount 2,000 × 1.1² = GH₵2,420, so the interest is GH₵420.\n\n**8.** 5,000 × 1.05² = GH₵5,512.50\n\n**9.** GH₵1,110\n\n**10.** Discount GH₵384, so GH₵2,816.\n\n#### Challenge\n\n**1.** Simple GH₵400; compound GH₵420; the difference of GH₵20 is the interest earned in the second year on the first year's GH₵200 of interest.\n\n**2.** The interest equals the principal, so P = P × R × 8 ÷ 100, giving R = 12.5% per annum.\n\n**3.** Total 180 worker-days; 180 ÷ 9 = 20 workers, so 8 more are needed.\n\n**4.** GH₵2,816 is 88% of the price, so the marked price is 2,816 ÷ 0.88 = GH₵3,200.\n\n**5.** (a) 8,000 × 1.05³ = GH₵9,261. (b) GH₵1,261. (c) Simple interest is GH₵1,200, so compound gives GH₵61 more.\n\n#### Applied task\n\n\n\n**1.** (a) 1,500 kg, 2,100 kg and 3,600 kg. (b) GH₵9,600, GH₵13,440 and GH₵23,040. (c) 8% of 23,040 = GH₵1,843.20, so he pays GH₵21,196.80 and the farmer loses GH₵1,843.20.\n\n**2.** (a) Interest 12,000 × 15 × 2 ÷ 100 = GH₵3,600, so GH₵15,600. (b) 12,000 × 1.13² = GH₵15,322.80. (c) Bank B is cheaper by GH₵277.20.\n\n**3.** (a) 12 × 6 = 72 worker-days for ⅓ of the job. (b) The whole job needs 216 worker-days. (c) 216 − 72 = 144 worker- days in 9 days, needing 16 workers — four more than at present.\n\n#### Exam-style\n\n**1.** GH₵1,500, GH₵2,100 and GH₵3,600 **[3]**\n\n**2.** 2.25 km **[3]**\n\n**3.** 15 hours **[3]**\n\n**4.** GH₵1,080 **[3]**\n\n**5.** GH₵420 **[4]**\n\n**6.** GH₵3,200 **[4]**\n\n#### Marking notes and common errors\n\n- **Direct or indirect?** Ask whether more of one means more or less of the other before any arithmetic. Treating an indirect problem as direct is the standard error.\n\n- **Worker-days.** Total work is workers × days and stays constant. This single idea answers every indirect proportion question in the syllabus.\n\n- **Compound interest.** Either work year by year or use P(1 + r/100)ⁿ. The year-by-year method is safer at this level and shows the examiner the reasoning.\n\n- **Challenge 4 and Exam 6.** The percentage is of the marked price, not of the price paid. Adding 12% to GH₵2,816 gives GH₵3,153.92, which is wrong.\n\n- **Money.** Two decimal places throughout, and the answer must carry GH₵.\n\n\n\n### Review 1 — Number\n\n*Chapters 1 to 5. Time: 45 minutes. Total: 30 marks.*\n\n**1.** (a) 5 (b) 24 (c) −4 **[3]**\n\n**2.** 3/11 **[3]**\n\n**3.** (a) 47.39 (b) 47.4 **[2]**\n\n**4.** 8.97 and 12 **[4]**\n\n**5.** (a) 5√2 (b) 5√2 **[3]**\n\n**6.** 2√3 **[3]**\n\n**7.** 1 5/24 and ¼ **[4]**\n\n**8.** 880, then 704 **[3]**\n\n**9.** GH₵1,500, GH₵2,100 and GH₵3,600 **[3]**\n\n**10.** GH₵420 **[2]**\n\n\n\n*Strand 2: Algebra*"
